0, x = 0
a, x = 0
is lower semicontinuous if a ≤ 0 (“jump down at x = 0 or no jump at all”), and is not lower semicontinuous if a > 0 (“jump up”).
The following statement links lower semicontinuity with the geometry of the epigraph.


